# Nuxt 4 conventions

- Vue app lives in `app/`. Do not put pages/components at the repo root.
- Components: PascalCase, two or more words. Auto-import by filename; do not edit component registries.
- `TrackCard` is presentational: props + emits, no `useFetch`, no store calls.
- Page data: `useFetch` / `useAsyncData`. Clicks and one-off calls: `$fetch`.
- Pinia: `modules: ["@pinia/nuxt"]` must stay at the **top level** of `nuxt.config.ts`, not inside `runtimeConfig`.
- Do not destructure store refs without `storeToRefs` — reactivity is lost.
- Call `usePlayerStore()` / `useFavoritesStore()` at setup top level, not inside click handlers.
- Styles: `<style scoped>`, BEM-ish (`block__element--modifier`). Match the file’s existing quote style; new files use `"`.
- Types: no `any` on API boundaries. Import `Track` from `~/utils/mock-tracks` until stage 11 moves it to `shared/`.
- Empty `.vue` files (0 bytes) break the build. A file referenced from a template must have `<template>` or `<script>`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
if (process.client) localStorage.getItem("x")

// ✅ GOOD
if (import.meta.client) localStorage.getItem("x")
```
